commit e140d940c5900dd2079fea07a11b422132fda182

C03: a capture order followed by «describeme lo que ves» is the screen-content reading (SCREEN1485)

SCREEN1423 left H0594 «Toma un screenshot de la pantalla ahora mismo y describeme lo que ves» conditioned: the strict catalog resolver returned a bare capture.screenshot (its description branch needs «describe» as a whole word, which «describeme» is not) and the implicit screen reading only accepted the bare «describe lo que ves». Both readers now treat a capture order followed by «describeme/decime lo que ves» or «describe what you see» as the screen-content reading of SCREEN1417 (reviewed capture then ocr.read, honest preface), without appending a second capture and without vision.describe, which has no provider on this PC. The «captura de pantalla» wording with that tail is still resolved by the enumerated-domain table as a bare capture (documented).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


